Subject: [PATCH 50/51] research38/38b/38c: row-split and row-pair K8V4 verify
 attention (NINFER_ATTN_ROWSPLIT=1|2|3)

The 16-column INT8-V verify tree of one row runs a row-split kernel (1 or 2 row tiles per CTA) or, with 3, a
row-pair kernel (one 16-row tile per CTA, eight warps scoring the split's key tiles in pairs). The new columns are
appended first by a 16-block kernel. Split partials are bit-identical, so the K8V4 reduce is unchanged. The next
GEMM's L2 fill (NINFER_L2_FILL bit 64) runs in grid z-slices past the slots.

Spec-Bench-480 unforced ids 482/482 identical; with research39, forced ms/round -0.72% / -0.58% (job 118b).
